      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 1.83,
          "en": "Now that you learned a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.83,
          "end": 3.9,
          "en": "about inputs and outputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.9,
          "end": 6.12,
          "en": "and how to build and use components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.12,
          "end": 9.12,
          "en": "it's time for a little exercise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.12,
          "end": 11.31,
          "en": "And my exercise for you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 11.31,
          "end": 14.7,
          "en": "is that you should replace this texture",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.7,
          "end": 18.603,
          "en": "with a separate component, a TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.25,
          "end": 22.92,
          "en": "which receives and outputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.92,
          "end": 26.133,
          "en": "the name of the user that is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.23,
          "end": 31.14,
          "en": "Now keep in mind that we are getting the information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.14,
          "end": 34.56,
          "en": "which user is selected here in the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.56,
          "end": 36.75,
          "en": "and it's also here in the AppComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.75,
          "end": 40.2,
          "en": "where you should then add this TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.2,
          "end": 43.98,
          "en": "which you should build for this exercise here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.98,
          "end": 47.433,
          "en": "so that you then output your TasksComponent here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.42,
          "end": 51.15,
          "en": "Of course, it doesn't exist yet at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 51.15,
          "end": 53.55,
          "en": "but you should build and output it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 53.55,
          "end": 58.55,
          "en": "and you should then pass the username to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.86,
          "end": 60.75,
          "en": "You don't have to worry about styling",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.75,
          "end": 62.34,
          "en": "or about any other features,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.34,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "but that's now an exercise for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 67.89,
          "en": "I'll give you a couple of seconds to pause the video",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.89,
          "end": 69.3,
          "en": "and try this on your own,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.3,
          "end": 72.603,
          "en": "and thereafter we'll implement this together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 75.63,
          "end": 80.1,
          "en": "So did you succeed? Let's try this together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.1,
          "end": 84.3,
          "en": "And for that I'll start by creating a new component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.3,
          "end": 86.25,
          "en": "and I will do that with help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 86.25,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "of the Angular CLI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.17,
          "end": 91.32,
          "en": "though you could of course also do it manually,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.32,
          "end": 95.19,
          "en": "but I'll generate a new component with ng g c,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 95.19,
          "end": 97.263,
          "en": "and I'll then name it tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.52000000000001,
          "end": 100.25999999999999,
          "en": "Now, here's also a little trick.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 100.25999999999999,
          "end": 104.7,
          "en": "You can add --skip-tests to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 104.7,
          "end": 108.24000000000001,
          "en": "that this testing file is not being generated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 108.24000000000001,
          "end": 110.31,
          "en": "because we don't need it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.31,
          "end": 114.18,
          "en": "Alternatively, we could of course also simply delete it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 116.64,
          "en": "but this will not create it in the first place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.64,
          "end": 120,
          "en": "And with that, therefore, I now got this tasks folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120,
          "end": 122.643,
          "en": "with those TasksComponent files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.02,
          "end": 128.4,
          "en": "and now it's in this tasks.component.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.4,
          "end": 131.82,
          "en": "where I wanna output the username, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.82,
          "end": 133.08,
          "en": "in an htwo element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.08,
          "end": 136.2,
          "en": "But it's totally up to you how you structure this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 136.2,
          "end": 137.67000000000002,
          "en": "and how you output this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 137.67000000000002,
          "end": 139.953,
          "en": "That's not what this exercise is about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 141.39,
          "end": 144.12,
          "en": "Now, for that, of course, we need to get the name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.12,
          "end": 146.22,
          "en": "of the user that should be output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 146.22,
          "end": 149.19,
          "en": "And since we have that information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 149.19,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "which user is selected in the AppComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 155.04,
          "en": "that means that in the TasksComponent",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.04,
          "end": 157.44,
          "en": "where we need that information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 157.44,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "we have to accept an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 163.82999999999998,
          "en": "So we should import this input decorator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.82999999999998,
          "end": 166.773,
          "en": "and add a new input property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 168.06,
          "end": 170.94,
          "en": "And that could now be the entire user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.94,
          "end": 173.52,
          "en": "It could be the userId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.52,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "and of course the name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 178.59,
          "en": "And we could then use that ID to select the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 178.59,
          "end": 181.17,
          "en": "from that DAMI users array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.17,
          "end": 184.62,
          "en": "But of course it could also just be the name of the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 184.62,
          "end": 186.543,
          "en": "and that's what I'll accept here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 187.47,
          "end": 191.28,
          "en": "Now, that should be a string and I know that I will get it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.28,
          "end": 193.41,
          "en": "but to ensure that I will get it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.41,
          "end": 195.63,
          "en": "I will add this configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 195.63,
          "end": 199.17000000000002,
          "en": "and set this to a required input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.17000000000002,
          "end": 203.55,
          "en": "Now, with that, we can go to this tasks.component.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.55,
          "end": 208.55,
          "en": "and then there use string interpolation to output that name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.67000000000002,
          "end": 213.72,
          "en": "And that's all we have to do in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.72,
          "end": 217.92000000000002,
          "en": "Now in the app.component.html file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 217.92000000000002,
          "end": 222.195,
          "en": "I am already trying to use the TasksComponent,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 222.195,
          "end": 223.77,
          "en": "but of course here I'm getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 223.77,
          "end": 226.053,
          "en": "that this is not a known element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 227.37,
          "end": 230.88,
          "en": "Now I can use this quick fix to automatically add it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 230.88,
          "end": 232.23,
          "en": "to the imports array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 232.23,
          "end": 234.93,
          "en": "or you can do this manually.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 234.93,
          "end": 236.64,
          "en": "Either way, you have to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.64,
          "end": 239.61,
          "en": "that in the AppComponents imports array here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.61,
          "end": 243.723,
          "en": "in the component decorator, this TasksComponent is added.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 244.92,
          "end": 247.2,
          "en": "And to be able to add it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 247.2,
          "end": 250.503,
          "en": "it also must be imported here at the top of the file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 251.58,
          "end": 254.7,
          "en": "Now in the AppComponent template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 254.7,
          "end": 258.66,
          "en": "we of course want to set this name property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.66,
          "end": 262.47,
          "en": "and I wanna set it to a dynamic value because it will change",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 262.47,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "whenever we select a different user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 267.36,
          "en": "Now for that, of course, as a first step",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 267.36,
          "end": 270.21,
          "en": "in the AppComponent class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 270.21,
          "end": 272.22,
          "en": "we have to make sure that we store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.22,
          "end": 275.403,
          "en": "that information, which user is selected.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 276.45,
          "end": 279.06,
          "en": "So we could add a selectedUser",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 279.06,
          "end": 283.803,
          "en": "or maybe a selectedUserId property, whatever you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 285,
          "end": 289.83,
          "en": "And initially set this to u1, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 289.83,
          "end": 291.36,
          "en": "if we're storing that ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 291.36,
          "end": 294.33,
          "en": "to initially store the first user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 294.33,
          "end": 296.58,
          "en": "Now here in onSelectUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 296.58,
          "end": 300.57,
          "en": "instead of console logging which user was selected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 300.57,
          "end": 304.26,
          "en": "we can set this selectedUserId equal to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 304.26,
          "end": 307.68,
          "en": "that ID we're receiving as a parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 307.68,
          "end": 311.1,
          "en": "Now, of course, in the template, we don't need the ID,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 311.1,
          "end": 313.837,
          "en": "but instead the name of the selectedUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 315.06,
          "end": 320.04,
          "en": "but we can now compute this by adding another property here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 320.04,
          "end": 323.49,
          "en": "a getter property with the get keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 323.49,
          "end": 325.533,
          "en": "which could be the selectedUser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 326.37,
          "end": 330.39300000000003,
          "en": "so that we also practice the usage of computed values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 331.47,
          "end": 334.59000000000003,
          "en": "And here I wanna return this.users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 334.59000000000003,
          "end": 337.44,
          "en": "which is my list of all the users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 337.44,
          "end": 342.44,
          "en": "And then I wanna find the user with this ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 342.78,
          "end": 345.03,
          "en": "And find, of course, is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 345.03,
          "end": 347.04,
          "en": "that's built into JavaScript.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 347.04,
          "end": 350.31,
          "en": "It's not Angular or TypeScript specific.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 350.31,
          "end": 351.9,
          "en": "Instead find allows us",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 351.9,
          "end": 356.9,
          "en": "to, well, find a specific element in an array of elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 357.87,
          "end": 361.17,
          "en": "For that, find takes a function as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 361.17,
          "end": 365.34,
          "en": "And that function then itself receives an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.34,
          "end": 368.01,
          "en": "which is the user it's currently looking at,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 368.01,
          "end": 370.59,
          "en": "because this function here will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 370.59,
          "end": 373.32,
          "en": "for all the elements in that array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.32,
          "end": 376.05,
          "en": "and it will then receive the individual element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 376.05,
          "end": 378.693,
          "en": "it's currently evaluating as an input.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 379.77,
          "end": 381.45,
          "en": "And we then have to return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 381.45,
          "end": 383.94,
          "en": "if that's the element we were looking for",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 383.94,
          "end": 386.46,
          "en": "or false otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 386.46,
          "end": 389.07,
          "en": "And therefore I wanna return true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 389.07,
          "end": 392.25,
          "en": "if the ID of the user I'm currently looking at",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 392.25,
          "end": 393.93,
          "en": "in that array of users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 393.93,
          "end": 398.183,
          "en": "if that's equal to the selectedUserId.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 400.2,
          "end": 402.447,
          "en": "And that's how we could dynamically compute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 402.447,
          "end": 406.837,
          "en": "the selectedUser and find that selectedUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 408.09000000000003,
          "end": 409.44,
          "en": "And therefore, now of course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 409.44,
          "end": 411.93,
          "en": "back in the AppComponent template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 411.93,
          "end": 415.05,
          "en": "we can use property binding here on name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 415.05,
          "end": 418.44,
          "en": "to set this equal to the selectedUser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 418.44,
          "end": 420.093,
          "en": "And then there the name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 421.8,
          "end": 425.37,
          "en": "Now you see I now actually get an error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
